            ["HelpText"] = "ShaderRipper — DXBC assembly / GLSL source -> ShaderLab + HLSLPROGRAM\n\nUsage:\n  ShaderRipper.exe --data <game _Data dir> [--out <output dir>] [options]\n  ShaderRipper.exe <game _Data dir> <output dir> [options]        (positional form, kept for compatibility)\n\nRequired:\n  --data <dir>          Game data directory (containing resources.assets); or set env var SHADERRIPPER_DATA\n  --file <path>         Input file(s) instead of a game dir: .assets SerializedFile,\n            .bundle/.assetbundle/.unity3d container, or .apk (Android). Repeatable, accepts\n            comma/semicolon lists and wildcards; a bare argument pointing at a file also works\n\nOutput (always an AssetRipper-style tree — Assets/Shader/<name>.shader, Assets/Resources/... for\n        Resources assets, bundle container paths honoured; copy it over an ExportedProject):\n  --out <dir>           Output directory; default ./<game name>_ShaderLabs (game name from app.info)\n            or set env var SHADERRIPPER_OUT\n\nResources (root of schema/data):\n  --root <dir>          Explicit path; by default searches upward from the exe dir, then the\n            working directory, for a directory containing schema/ or data/ (or ShaderRipper.csproj)\n            or set env var SHADERRIPPER_ROOT\n  --schema <file|dir>   Shader type tree (auto-selected by SerializedFile version by default)\n  --names <dir>         $Globals fix-up table directory (default data/globals_names when present; shipped builds may omit it)\n  --builtin-index <f>   Built-in shader list (default data/unity_builtin_shaders.txt)\n  --matrix-names <f>    float4x4 name list (default data/unity_matrix_names.txt)\n  --tmp-layouts <dir>   $Globals layout table directory (default data/tmp_layouts)\n\nFiltering/debug:\n  --only <substr>       Only process shaders whose name contains this substring\n  --dump [substr]       Print blob/param-block info only, write no output\n  --list-shaders <file> List all shader names in a SerializedFile\n  --bundles [dir]       Scan asset bundles, optionally in another directory (default same as --data)\n  --platform <id|name>  Force a backend (d3d11/d3d9/gles3/gles20/openglcore/metal/vulkan...);\n            default picks d3d11 (assembly -> HLSL transliteration); GLSL source from\n            GLES3/GLES2/OpenGLCore/legacy GL is translated back to HLSLPROGRAM by the built-in\n            translator and auto-selected when no d3d11 slot exists; d3d9 (SM2/3) and\n            D3D12 (DXIL) get native disassembly only, into Disassembly/;\n            Metal/Vulkan are also reference-only\n  --asm                 Emit per-instruction disassembly comments (default off);\n            d3d11 = DXBC instruction comments, glsl/gles = original GLSL line comments,\n            d3d9/d3d12 = native disassembly (into comments and Disassembly/)\n  --asm-parser <regex|antlr>  Which route reads the DXBC disassembly (default regex):\n            regex = hand-written scanner;  antlr = the bundled DxbcAsm.g4 grammar.\n            Both produce the same model (verified on 75,919 files); this is a\n            mechanism choice, not an output choice\n  --glsl-parser <antlr|regex>  Which route reads the GLSL payload (default antlr):\n            antlr = the bundled Glsl.g4 grammar;  regex = the line scanner.\n            Both produce the same text (verified on 3,164 files, and byte-identical\n            on a full GL export); the grammar route is the default because it reads\n            statements, not physical lines\n  --validate           Re-parse each emitted shader with the bundled ANTLR grammars\n            (ShaderLab + HLSL) and report any that is not well-formed\n  --no-tmp-layout       Do not use the $Globals layout tables (TMP row numbers stay numeric)\n  --syntax <hlsl|cg>    Dialect of the emitted program block (default hlsl):\n            hlsl = HLSLPROGRAM with Texture2D/SamplerState + .Sample()/.SampleLevel()\n            cg   = CGPROGRAM with sampler2D + tex2D/tex2Dlod (the legacy form)\n\nDiagnostics:\n  --disasm <file>       Disassemble a single program file (DXBC/DXIL container or d3d9 token stream)\n  --glsl2cg <file>      Translate a single GLSL file back to HLSL (add --asm for original-line comments)\n  --lang <en|zh>        UI language (default: system UI language)\n  -h, --help            Show this help\n",
